WEBVTT

00:07.700 --> 00:10.690
Fall in love, boys and girls

00:11.300 --> 00:14.360
Twinkle! Put a star in your eye

00:15.000 --> 00:17.940
The passion, the way it was born

00:18.580 --> 00:21.340
Makes sparks in the jungle! Haré+Guu!

00:21.980 --> 00:25.140
How the hips shake, mucho dizzying

00:25.580 --> 00:28.710
Amigo, that's risky for a kid

00:29.420 --> 00:32.390
If I were to kiss, I'd get sucked in

00:33.060 --> 00:35.420
Tonight, I want to see something scary

00:36.430 --> 00:38.460
Don't be afraid

00:38.460 --> 00:40.260
Going from one push after another

00:40.260 --> 00:42.030
The surprising feeling is nice

00:42.030 --> 00:43.700
And you end up dancing till morning

00:43.700 --> 00:45.440
LOVE LOVE LOVE

00:45.440 --> 00:48.960
TROPICANA

00:50.840 --> 00:54.000
Catch me in the shade under the palm tree

00:54.510 --> 00:57.640
Make me wait, more than down to the limit

00:58.250 --> 01:01.310
I'm sorry, but you're already addicted

01:01.920 --> 01:05.010
From the jungle you can't escape! Haré+Guu!

01:05.660 --> 01:08.450
Fall in love, boys and girls

01:08.960 --> 01:11.930
Twinkle! Put a star in your eye

01:12.730 --> 01:15.700
The passion, the way it was born

01:16.330 --> 01:18.300
Makes sparks in the jungle! Haré+Guu!

01:38.040 --> 01:39.440
I'm so jealous...

01:39.870 --> 01:41.770
Is something wrong with that photo book?

01:41.880 --> 01:44.940
The scenery covered in snow
is just so wonderful!

01:45.350 --> 01:46.000
I see...

01:46.080 --> 01:49.050
Oh, just for once, I want to see snow!

01:49.050 --> 01:50.220
I want to touch it!

01:50.220 --> 01:52.740
True... I wonder how it feels.

01:52.820 --> 01:54.350
Snow, huh...

01:54.350 --> 01:56.520
I want to play around in the snow once.

01:56.520 --> 01:58.550
It's something you can
never do in a jungle, right?

01:59.890 --> 02:01.620
That's true, but...

02:03.860 --> 02:07.830
The biggest problem I have is that in a
jungle, you can't wear cute coats!

02:07.830 --> 02:09.270
That's the biggest one?

02:20.110 --> 02:23.840
Why can't there be some wonderful miracle
that would make it snow in the jungle?

02:24.480 --> 02:26.750
That way, I'd be able
to go out wearing a coat!

02:27.590 --> 02:30.080
I don't want it to snow just for your coat!

02:30.420 --> 02:31.480
Coat...

02:31.790 --> 02:34.590
Geez, your thinking is so childish...
It's immature.

02:34.590 --> 02:36.080
But then, we are still children.

02:38.900 --> 02:41.890
We're going to start class. Get to your seats.

02:42.770 --> 02:44.290
Now, this period is...

02:44.470 --> 02:45.940
...a nap!

02:46.110 --> 02:47.110
He's sleepy, huh...

02:47.110 --> 02:48.240
Study hall again?

02:48.240 --> 02:49.340
Just as always...

02:49.340 --> 02:51.000
Or rather, he just came here
to get his pillow?

02:52.850 --> 02:55.450
Of course, I'd like to ride on a sleigh.

02:55.450 --> 02:57.250
Ski jumps, and aerial loops!

02:57.250 --> 02:59.240
They look like it'd hurt if you fell.

03:00.750 --> 03:04.380
I made this coat with an image of a
precocious little fairy...

03:04.460 --> 03:05.650
It's so cute!

03:06.430 --> 03:10.100
Well, Ravenna, I think this one would look
good on you! Don't you think?

03:10.100 --> 03:12.120
Doesn't it look like a
French schoolgirl's winter uniform?

03:12.230 --> 03:13.700
T-That's true.

03:13.870 --> 03:16.400
There's no way it'd
snow in the jungle, though.

03:16.400 --> 03:17.840
Really, kids are so optimistic nowadays.

03:18.100 --> 03:19.830
It's fine. They have
something to dream about.

03:19.970 --> 03:21.530
A dream? Of snow?

03:22.210 --> 03:23.440
Snow, huh...

03:25.450 --> 03:27.210
But I don't like the cold...

03:27.280 --> 03:29.750
I prefer the jungle warm.

03:36.260 --> 03:38.050
Oh, geez, I'm going to sleep.

03:40.660 --> 03:42.820
It's getting really cold all of a sudden...

03:43.030 --> 03:44.620
Maybe a squall is on its way over.

03:44.800 --> 03:46.770
It feels worse than that!

03:48.270 --> 03:49.330
It's strange.

03:49.440 --> 03:50.990
Now that you mention it, my breath...

03:52.340 --> 03:54.170
H-Hey, guys! Look outside!

03:56.980 --> 03:57.810
Snow...

04:04.020 --> 04:05.180
...has piled up!

04:06.590 --> 04:07.750
Y-You're kidding! Why!?

04:07.850 --> 04:08.860
You're serious!?

04:08.860 --> 04:10.290
When did all this pile up?

04:10.660 --> 04:12.260
More importantly, it's cold!

04:12.260 --> 04:15.060
When I know that snow really has fallen,
it feels even colder!

04:15.160 --> 04:17.860
B-But I didn't see any of this falling...

04:20.130 --> 04:21.120
Guu did this!?

04:26.740 --> 04:27.740
It couldn't be...

04:27.740 --> 04:28.830
I haven't said anything yet.

04:29.310 --> 04:30.330
Well, to put it one way...

04:31.110 --> 04:32.910
...a miracle has occurred.

04:33.250 --> 04:34.040
A miracle?

04:34.110 --> 04:34.750
A miracle!

04:34.750 --> 04:36.270
This is some cheap miracle we've got here.

04:36.380 --> 04:37.720
But still, this is the first snow!

04:37.720 --> 04:39.690
I don't care if it's a miracle or not,
let's go play!

04:40.120 --> 04:41.420
Hey, Gupta!

04:41.420 --> 04:42.010
What is it!?

04:42.290 --> 04:45.330
I hear snow is really cold, so we have to
at least get some shoes on.

04:45.330 --> 04:46.160
Good point.

04:47.660 --> 04:51.260
He's the most enthusiastic of all of us,
despite treating you like a little kid, Marie.

04:51.330 --> 04:53.860
Hey! Hey! We should hurry outside, too!

05:00.210 --> 05:01.570
So pretty...

05:09.820 --> 05:11.720
Amazing! Real snow!

05:11.790 --> 05:12.910
So cold!

05:13.720 --> 05:15.310
Oh, it's cold!

05:15.690 --> 05:17.020
Hey, look, look!

05:17.020 --> 05:17.090
Let me see... Wah! It's cold!

05:17.090 --> 05:18.720
It's cold, and it's fluffy!

05:18.830 --> 05:19.590
Let me see...

05:19.590 --> 05:21.420
Wah! It's cold!

05:21.490 --> 05:22.360
So this is snow!

05:22.360 --> 05:23.060
So this is snow!
You know...

05:23.230 --> 05:25.060
You're right! It's fluffy!
All of you, let's think hard about this, like...

05:25.330 --> 05:27.870
"Why is it snowing in the jungle?" or...

05:27.870 --> 05:29.330
"What's the reason behind this?"

05:29.400 --> 05:31.440
The fact that I'm the only one
thinking about it is ridiculous!

05:31.440 --> 05:32.170
But, you know...

05:32.940 --> 05:36.770
I'm glad that I was able to haveall of you
wear the winter outfits that I made.

05:37.580 --> 05:40.170
But why did it snow so suddenly?

05:40.280 --> 05:41.610
Even if you call it a miracle...

05:41.610 --> 05:43.310
That's true. I wonder why!

05:45.350 --> 05:47.110
That's right! That's precisely it!

05:47.320 --> 05:49.520
I don't know what she means
by making it snow...

05:49.520 --> 05:51.920
...but these guys won't believe
so easily that it's some miracle!

05:52.590 --> 05:53.990
That, of course...

05:56.000 --> 05:58.460
...is a gift from God.

05:59.270 --> 06:00.600
From God?

06:00.670 --> 06:01.570
A gift?

06:01.870 --> 06:02.990
So it IS a miracle...

06:03.070 --> 06:04.260
All of you are too innocent.

06:06.710 --> 06:09.140
By the way, what kind of games
do you play in the snow?

06:09.140 --> 06:12.040
This is our first snow, so I'm not sure.

06:12.110 --> 06:13.370
How should we play?

06:13.650 --> 06:14.200
I know!

06:14.710 --> 06:15.520
Hey, Haré!

06:15.520 --> 06:18.880
Weda originally came from the city, so she
knows what winter is like, right?

06:18.990 --> 06:21.350
You never heard about snow, Haré?

06:22.420 --> 06:25.230
That's right! You know
something right? Tell us!

06:25.230 --> 06:26.020
Tell us!

06:26.430 --> 06:28.390
T-They're expecting something out of me...

06:28.530 --> 06:29.960
Well, I don't feel bad about this...

06:30.360 --> 06:32.890
...but all things considered,
I really hate the cold...

06:33.030 --> 06:34.400
Come to think of it, Mom...

06:34.400 --> 06:36.390
Then, I'll tell you.

06:37.140 --> 06:37.830
You serious?

06:37.900 --> 06:40.870
How about a snowman for starters?

06:41.270 --> 06:42.100
A snowman?

06:42.240 --> 06:43.730
I think I've seen that in a book somewhere!

06:43.980 --> 06:46.170
I wonder what they're like in real life?

06:46.750 --> 06:48.740
So this is the feeling of being left out...

06:48.820 --> 06:50.980
I'll make one as an example.

06:52.250 --> 06:52.910
Fine.

06:55.160 --> 06:56.060
Amazing!

06:56.060 --> 06:56.920
That looks hard!

06:56.920 --> 06:58.480
I see, so this is a snowman...

06:58.560 --> 07:00.530
Guu is more skilled than I thought.

07:01.090 --> 07:02.530
Now, all of you...

07:02.700 --> 07:04.090
...can try making your own.

07:05.630 --> 07:06.560
That's not right!

07:07.030 --> 07:09.520
And, in the case of a celebration,
you fill in eyes with coal.

07:09.600 --> 07:10.630
That's even more wrong!

07:10.970 --> 07:13.270
What, you want to join the group?

07:13.810 --> 07:14.570
I feel humiliated!

07:14.770 --> 07:16.400
Let's make a huge one!

07:16.480 --> 07:17.500
My hands are cold!

07:17.710 --> 07:18.800
Hey hey hey hey, guys!

07:18.880 --> 07:20.510
T-There's something called a snowfight!

07:20.580 --> 07:21.480
Why don't we do that?

07:21.480 --> 07:22.580
A snowfight?

07:22.580 --> 07:25.240
I heard from Mom that it warms you up.

07:25.420 --> 07:27.440
And everyone can participate!

07:28.760 --> 07:29.650
Then, let's play that!

07:29.760 --> 07:30.690
Yeah! Let's do it!

07:33.430 --> 07:36.760
You form two teams in a snowfight, right?

07:36.830 --> 07:40.820
I think so. But I'm not sure of
what to do from there.

07:40.970 --> 07:43.400
Come to think of it,
I wonder what the rules are...

07:43.540 --> 07:46.660
W-Well, we make snowballs...

07:46.840 --> 07:49.870
...and hurl them at your enemies
with all your strength.

07:50.180 --> 07:51.440
With full strength?

07:51.610 --> 07:54.510
Correct! You win when all
of your opponents stop moving.

07:54.610 --> 07:56.050
Were the rules that dangerous?

07:56.950 --> 07:59.210
On a side note, to insure victory...

07:59.290 --> 08:03.790
...you can cram rocks inside the snowball to
strike the opponent more effectively...

08:03.790 --> 08:05.760
All right! Let's hurry up and get started!

08:09.000 --> 08:10.290
All right, let's begin!

08:12.130 --> 08:15.100
ALL WHITE

09:14.930 --> 09:15.760
So fun!

09:15.760 --> 09:16.920
This is fun!

09:18.400 --> 09:19.160
Right, Haré?

09:19.430 --> 09:20.830
Y-You're right.

09:21.200 --> 09:23.530
She's right. It's more fun than I thought.

09:23.740 --> 09:26.860
I hate the cold, and it's nothing more than
throwing snowballs at each other...

09:27.440 --> 09:29.000
How is it? Isn't it fun?

09:29.240 --> 09:30.440
Y-Yeah...

09:30.940 --> 09:32.070
You're not alone.

09:32.280 --> 09:35.370
The fact that you have friends next to you
makes a difference.

09:35.920 --> 09:36.640
Guu...

09:36.920 --> 09:39.580
You made it snow here just to make me
realize that?

09:43.460 --> 09:44.660
All right! Let's do it again!

09:44.660 --> 09:45.430
Yay!

09:45.430 --> 09:46.590
Let's switch the teams around!

09:47.130 --> 09:49.820
Oh, but we're running out of snow...

09:49.960 --> 09:51.900
You're right. I think it's melting.

09:52.070 --> 09:54.590
It's melting away already?

10:01.210 --> 10:03.700
It's kinda sad to see it melt...

10:04.010 --> 10:05.480
I wish more of it would fall.

10:15.520 --> 10:16.390
Snow!

10:16.390 --> 10:17.750
Snow is falling!

10:21.130 --> 10:22.560
You're right!

10:22.560 --> 10:25.870
Wow, this is the first time I've seen snow fall!

10:25.870 --> 10:27.960
Snow! Snow!

10:28.030 --> 10:28.670
Guu...

10:28.670 --> 10:29.690
Hurray!

10:35.580 --> 10:36.800
S-So cold!

10:37.510 --> 10:39.210
I feel like I'll get blown away!

10:39.650 --> 10:42.140
This is no good, Haré!
Let's go back to the classroom!

10:42.520 --> 10:43.640
You went too far!

10:54.160 --> 10:55.320
It's cold!

10:55.400 --> 10:57.160
We've got the shutters closed
and it's still this cold?

10:57.300 --> 10:58.960
It really is cold!

10:59.470 --> 11:00.450
I wonder when it will stop falling?

11:00.570 --> 11:02.300
It looks like it's falling even harder now.

11:02.440 --> 11:04.130
But it's pretty strange...

11:04.400 --> 11:08.600
It started falling right when we started
thinking that we wanted more snow.

11:10.440 --> 11:11.570
It's wonderful!

11:12.080 --> 11:17.740
I mean, the falling snow is like little fairies
that come down to heal people's hearts.

11:18.080 --> 11:22.460
The deeper the people's sorrows are, the
more sinful the people are...

11:22.460 --> 11:25.550
...the heavier and harder the snow falls.

11:25.630 --> 11:26.960
I don't like that setting.

11:27.330 --> 11:30.120
You know, we can't get out
until this blizzard is over.

11:30.200 --> 11:31.930
Will we have to stay in the school overnight?

11:32.100 --> 11:35.530
No way! It's too cold here,
and we have no food!

11:38.810 --> 11:42.300
But, to ask Guu to
stop this after everything...

11:42.440 --> 11:43.280
You're probably right.

11:43.280 --> 11:44.800
I haven't said anything yet!

11:45.650 --> 11:47.170
B-But, what should I do?

11:47.250 --> 11:49.740
If everyone found out that
this blizzard was my fault...

11:49.850 --> 11:51.480
What happens if we all get stranded here!?

11:51.550 --> 11:52.250
It's cold...

11:52.320 --> 11:53.840
I'm getting sleepy...

11:53.920 --> 11:55.650
If I die, I'll come back and haunt you!

11:55.720 --> 11:57.520
We'll come out to curse you, Haré!

11:57.620 --> 12:00.150
Your family is cursed
for generations to come!

12:00.230 --> 12:00.830
Not good!

12:00.830 --> 12:03.300
Maybe it's because of the cold,
but my thoughts are getting
more and more negative!

12:03.430 --> 12:04.060
You know...

12:04.060 --> 12:05.500
You know, don't you, Haré?

12:05.870 --> 12:07.990
I'm sure he doesn't know about Santa Claus.

12:08.370 --> 12:09.540
I heard that on a snowy day...

12:09.540 --> 12:14.870
...a person named Santa Claus comes to
drop off gifts to children!

12:14.940 --> 12:16.670
I heard about that, too!

12:16.740 --> 12:21.180
I believe it was an old man on a sleigh, and
he sneaks into your house late at night!

12:21.480 --> 12:22.550
Eh? Why?

12:22.550 --> 12:24.140
He should come by in the afternoon!

12:24.380 --> 12:25.490
That's because it's a fairy tale...

12:25.490 --> 12:27.750
It's because he has shameful motives.

12:28.120 --> 12:29.350
Oh, that makes sense.

12:30.020 --> 12:33.050
I don't like the idea of an old man sneaking
into your house late at night.

12:33.260 --> 12:35.420
But, he gives us gifts!

12:35.500 --> 12:36.430
You're an idiot.

12:36.600 --> 12:38.620
There's nothing more expensive than
something that's free.

12:38.870 --> 12:41.860
Why does someone who has absolutely
no relationship to you whatsoever
want to give you something?

12:42.470 --> 12:45.800
So, what's this Santa Claus guy look like?

12:46.240 --> 12:51.200
Well, he has a long white beard,
and wears red and white clothes.

12:57.450 --> 12:59.010
He comes on a snowy day, right?

13:07.230 --> 13:08.450
That's no joke!

13:08.530 --> 13:12.330
And, when he finds kids,
he tries to give them gifts, right?

13:21.810 --> 13:23.710
I wonder what the gifts are like.

13:32.650 --> 13:33.680
Scary!

13:33.820 --> 13:35.480
I wonder what would happen
if you said you didn't want it...

13:55.880 --> 13:56.780
I've got it!

13:56.780 --> 13:57.770
What?

13:58.180 --> 14:01.350
You said Santa Claus wears a red outfit,
right?

14:01.350 --> 14:02.410
Y-Yeah...

14:03.420 --> 14:06.110
I'm sure it's an outfit that's been dyed with
children's blood!

14:06.450 --> 14:08.820
Come on, of all things, that is...

14:09.720 --> 14:11.750
That's enough, okay? Stop it...

14:11.820 --> 14:13.310
They really believe it?

14:13.690 --> 14:15.830
You know, how about you
say something about it, Guu...

14:15.830 --> 14:17.520
Wait, you're all ready
to scare them, aren't you!?

14:17.660 --> 14:17.990
Yeah.

14:18.130 --> 14:20.170
Don't "Yeah!"
And where did you find that outfit!?

14:20.170 --> 14:20.930
Hurray!

14:21.000 --> 14:22.400
You did that routine already!

14:23.500 --> 14:24.330
Eh? You're kidding!

14:24.400 --> 14:25.560
Did someone turn them off?

14:25.640 --> 14:27.900
Oh no, it's not turning on.
It looks like we've got a power outage.

14:28.170 --> 14:30.670
We've gotten more
into the atmosphere now...

14:32.480 --> 14:34.240
I beg you, please stay quiet!!

14:34.750 --> 14:36.770
Hey, guys! Don't you hear something?

14:39.090 --> 14:39.950
What is that?

14:40.020 --> 14:41.250
Footsteps!

14:41.320 --> 14:42.310
Nooo!

14:42.420 --> 14:43.850
Guu! Is that you again!?

14:44.060 --> 14:46.460
As you can see, Guu is right here.

14:47.090 --> 14:48.360
Then... it's...

14:59.070 --> 15:00.560
What are all of you doing?

15:02.340 --> 15:03.740
It's rather cold out.

15:03.740 --> 15:04.970
And the lights are all out...

15:05.280 --> 15:07.300
In any case, we have to deal with the cold.

15:07.380 --> 15:09.510
When it's this cold,
if you fall asleep, you'll die.

15:09.580 --> 15:11.050
But, I want to sleep.

15:11.120 --> 15:12.240
But, if I do, I'll die.

15:12.320 --> 15:13.550
But, I want to sleep.

15:13.620 --> 15:16.020
But, if I do, I'll die.

15:16.190 --> 15:16.780
But, I want to sleep...

15:16.990 --> 15:19.390
Come on! You said you would die
if you fell asleep! Don't sleep!!

15:19.460 --> 15:20.860
I wonder if I could sleep if I died.

15:20.930 --> 15:21.890
That's not called sleeping!

15:21.890 --> 15:23.100
Then, I'll sleep, then die.

15:23.100 --> 15:25.290
I don't understand you! Hey! Wake up!

15:26.000 --> 15:29.060
Come to think of it, I'm getting sleepy, too.

15:29.300 --> 15:30.270
Me, too.

15:30.500 --> 15:32.730
N-No... Me, too...

15:34.010 --> 15:36.130
At this rate, everyone will freeze to death!

15:36.210 --> 15:37.300
I have to do something!

15:37.480 --> 15:38.670
C-Come to think of it...

15:38.740 --> 15:40.230
Wasn't there something called the
dumpling pushover (oshikura manju)?

15:40.310 --> 15:41.750
To blow away the cold.

15:42.280 --> 15:44.340
Dumpling pushover? What's that?

15:44.580 --> 15:45.140
Well...

15:45.450 --> 15:47.480
I wonder if you make dumplings?

15:47.550 --> 15:51.850
I get it. You forget about the cold because
you concentrate on cooking.

15:51.920 --> 15:55.520
Dumplings, huh...
That sounds good... I'm hungry.

15:55.590 --> 15:57.790
If anything, I like those
hot springs dumplings.

15:57.900 --> 16:00.630
A hot spring sounds good. It must be warm.

16:00.830 --> 16:02.770
But what's a pushover (oshikura)?

16:05.670 --> 16:06.940
A vegetable that's sticky
when you chop it up.

16:06.940 --> 16:07.700
That's an okra.
A vegetable that's sticky
when you chop it up.

16:08.070 --> 16:08.710
Dead people visiting
you when you're asleep?

16:08.710 --> 16:09.870
A dream visit (yume makura).
Dead people visiting
you when you're asleep?

16:10.010 --> 16:11.640
Somehow feeling nothing
will get better in the future.

16:11.640 --> 16:12.740
The future is pitch black (osaki makkura).
Somehow feeling nothing
will get better in the future.

16:16.080 --> 16:18.740
Argh! I've made them
colder and sleepier! What do I do!?

16:18.820 --> 16:21.050
T-T-T-Then, well, what about a dry towel rub?

16:21.120 --> 16:23.490
I heard from Mom that it
works fighting cold weather...

16:23.920 --> 16:25.080
Dry towel rub?

16:25.320 --> 16:26.220
You've heard of it?

16:26.290 --> 16:26.920
Nope.

16:27.290 --> 16:28.660
A dry towel rub (kanpu masatsu)...

16:28.660 --> 16:31.930
That is, to absolutely
take down your opponent.

16:31.930 --> 16:33.830
In other words,
complete annihilation (kanpu massatsu)!

16:34.430 --> 16:35.460
When you're a guy...

16:35.570 --> 16:39.230
...there are times when you have to fight,
knowing that you're going to lose...

16:39.310 --> 16:41.270
Even if you know you're going to die.

16:41.340 --> 16:43.170
You can't prevent yourself from freezing
unless you do that, right?

16:43.240 --> 16:45.110
W-Wait a minute, guys! Are you serious?

16:45.340 --> 16:47.440
No one will even collect
your body after you die.

16:47.510 --> 16:49.320
That's the principle of complete annihilation.

16:49.320 --> 16:50.540
Don't encourage them!

16:50.720 --> 16:51.720
H-Hey, guys! Look around!

16:51.720 --> 16:53.020
You're all acting weird because of the cold!

16:53.020 --> 16:55.010
Calm down!
All of you are just being fooled by Guu!

16:56.590 --> 16:57.720
What, it's just a lie?

16:57.720 --> 16:58.550
Yup, yup, a lie. A lie!

16:59.090 --> 17:00.490
Geez, what a waste of time!

17:01.860 --> 17:05.590
This is what happens when you try to show
off half-baked knowledge.

17:05.660 --> 17:07.060
Remember that.

17:12.910 --> 17:14.810
It's a relief to have some light.

17:15.140 --> 17:17.470
It's a good thing I kept candles
here for emergencies.

17:18.080 --> 17:19.040
That's right.

17:19.310 --> 17:21.180
In a story that I read the other day...

17:21.680 --> 17:24.310
...there was a really poor girl.

17:28.620 --> 17:31.590
And on a cold, snowy night...

17:31.590 --> 17:34.890
...she tried to keep
warm by lighting matches.

17:36.400 --> 17:41.890
When she did, lots of things that
she wanted came out of the matchlight.

17:42.670 --> 17:44.140
That's a good story.

17:44.540 --> 17:45.770
Things that she wanted, huh...

17:45.970 --> 17:49.110
Scrumptious meals, warm blankets...

17:49.110 --> 17:50.040
How wonderful...

17:51.180 --> 17:52.540
From the flame...

17:52.750 --> 17:53.730
How nice...

17:54.380 --> 17:55.540
A miracle...

17:56.720 --> 17:58.240
Wait, a bonfire!?

17:58.480 --> 17:59.490
What's that about a miracle!

17:59.490 --> 18:02.520
What's that about a feast inside a flame!?

18:02.520 --> 18:04.060
Don't lie, dammit!

18:04.060 --> 18:05.890
You all just caught some strange radio wave!

18:05.890 --> 18:07.260
You too!

18:07.330 --> 18:09.350
It's nothing but a broadcast
created by our brains!

18:11.030 --> 18:12.770
G-Guys! Get a grip!

18:12.770 --> 18:14.260
Out of the way!

18:15.030 --> 18:16.260
Dammit!!!

18:19.310 --> 18:21.770
Oh, every one of them has snapped...

18:22.140 --> 18:23.770
You're the only one that can save them.

18:24.440 --> 18:27.570
And so, Haré has volunteered
to go outside to find some help.

18:28.280 --> 18:28.840
Go ahead and go.

18:28.950 --> 18:31.080
Wait a minute here!
I'm saying I don't like the cold...

18:32.250 --> 18:35.950
You've liked being in situations like this
through the course of this series, right?

18:43.230 --> 18:45.130
Why is it always me?

18:45.300 --> 18:49.500
Hold on a sec, what am I going to use this
plush toy that I got from Marie for?

18:53.640 --> 18:56.700
I've heard this sound before...

18:56.980 --> 18:58.030
Haven't I?

19:01.310 --> 19:05.610
A white version of the big, black, hard, shiny
smelly, thing that makes a strange noise
- or rather, a polar bear!?

19:16.100 --> 19:17.390
I'm saved!

19:19.930 --> 19:21.590
I think I've sprained my foot...

19:22.300 --> 19:23.730
I can't walk anymore.

19:24.400 --> 19:26.470
Mom... I'm sorry, Mom...

19:26.470 --> 19:28.100
I can't move one more step...

19:29.010 --> 19:32.030
I can't reach wherever
you are anymore, Mom...

19:33.450 --> 19:34.810
People say that right before you die...

19:34.810 --> 19:38.410
...you see your life scroll by, as if you were
watching it on a revolving internal...

19:41.720 --> 19:42.290
What the hell!?

19:42.290 --> 19:46.090
Why are all my memories
about me and Guu!?

19:48.260 --> 19:49.350
Oh, a light!?

19:49.560 --> 19:50.460
I'm saved!

19:50.930 --> 19:53.930
E-Excuse me, can you help me...

19:53.930 --> 19:55.130
Are you a traveler?

19:56.340 --> 19:57.500
Who are you!?

19:57.500 --> 20:00.340
Well now, how nice of you
to stop by in this snow.

20:00.440 --> 20:01.840
You're the one that kicked me out!

20:01.840 --> 20:03.430
Now, I'm sure you must be hungry.

20:03.740 --> 20:07.410
I can't give you a proper treatment,
but come now... relax.

20:07.650 --> 20:09.670
What? You have some food?

20:10.850 --> 20:11.320
Have this.

20:11.380 --> 20:12.440
Are you mocking me!?

20:12.520 --> 20:14.210
I see, you don't care for this...

20:14.490 --> 20:14.920
Then...

20:14.920 --> 20:15.820
That's the same thing!

20:16.020 --> 20:18.580
I guess I will just have
to go prepare something.

20:19.190 --> 20:23.530
But please make sure to not
peek in while I'm preparing it.

20:23.800 --> 20:24.790
S-Sure...

20:25.530 --> 20:27.690
Wait a minute, was there
a place like this earlier?

20:30.440 --> 20:31.300
This is...

20:31.300 --> 20:32.360
From how things are going...

20:32.570 --> 20:33.500
It can't be!

20:33.570 --> 20:34.800
Hey, Guu! Stop it!

20:34.870 --> 20:35.340
Oh!

20:36.180 --> 20:37.610
Don't make such dramatic jokes!

20:37.910 --> 20:40.500
That's why I told you to not peek...

20:55.390 --> 20:58.920
Usually, things like this
end up being dreams.

20:59.370 --> 21:02.600
You know, like you wake up
in your bed, and think how glad you are
that it was all a dream.

21:08.640 --> 21:09.470
A dream...

21:09.540 --> 21:11.340
It was all a dream, Mom...

21:16.320 --> 21:17.580
Mom...

21:19.280 --> 21:20.650
Snow, huh?

22:34.990 --> 22:35.390
NEXT EPISODE

22:36.250 --> 22:37.400
Eh? We're going back to your old home!?

22:37.410 --> 22:39.580
Argh! Sheesh, really!
This is so sudden that my head is spinning and can't keep up!

22:39.590 --> 22:40.980
but we're just going to make a short visit and come back, right?

22:40.990 --> 22:41.870
Yeah, that's got to be it.

22:41.890 --> 22:45.370
I should properly introduce myself to my grandmother for once, as her grandson.

22:45.390 --> 22:46.350
I'm so stupid to jump to conclusions.

22:46.350 --> 22:47.290
I'm so stupid to jump to conclusions.

22:47.790 --> 22:50.020
I never mentioned anything
about returning to the jungle, did I?

22:50.020 --> 22:50.320
Eh?

22:50.320 --> 22:52.230
Geez, Haré, you jump
to conclusions too much.

22:52.230 --> 22:53.460
I didn't hear anything
about NOT returning, either!

22:53.460 --> 22:54.190
So, that means, for real...

22:54.190 --> 22:55.500
Yeah, saying goodbye for good.

22:55.500 --> 22:57.330
Wait a minute! All things considered,
this is too sudden!

22:57.400 --> 22:58.860
You're going to make
me cry in the end, dammit!

22:59.100 --> 23:01.070
Next episode of Haré+Guu:

23:01.070 --> 23:03.400
"Airport 21: Japanese Food and Western Food"

23:03.400 --> 23:04.500
Don't move the story along!

23:04.500 --> 23:05.010
Yeah!

23:07.110 --> 23:08.040
NEXT EPISODE

23:08.040 --> 23:09.210
Eh? We're going back to your old home!?

23:09.210 --> 23:11.350
Argh! Sheesh, really! This is so sudden that my head is spinning and can't
keep up!

23:11.350 --> 23:12.780
Oh, but we're just going to make a short visit and come back, right?

23:12.780 --> 23:13.680
Yeah, that's got to be it.

23:13.680 --> 23:15.990
I should properly introduce myself to my grandmother for once, as her
grandson.
